/* the flags this chapter adds to RFNAMEG/RFCNAMEG (chapter 2): */
RFPROC    // create a new (child) process; otherwise the CALLER's own
          //   resources are modified in place, no fork happens
RFFDG     // child gets an independent COPY of the descriptor table
          //   (same open channels, independent numbering from here on)
RFCFDG    // child starts with an EMPTY descriptor table
RFENVG    // child gets an independent COPY of /env (was: shared)
RFCENVG   // child starts with an EMPTY /env
RFMEM     // child SHARES data+bss with the parent (stack is always
          //   copy-on-write regardless); valid only together with RFPROC

